events.description:
This collaborative event brings together the community-powered film screenings and participatory storytelling of Scribe Video Center’s Street Movies! with the inaugural summer documentary series Black Earth, City Roots, presented by the Black Earth Urban Ag Hub. The series highlights urban agriculture in Philadelphia, Black agrarian futures, and the city’s legacies of resilience. Through film, conversation, and collective reflection, the gathering invites neighbors to connect across shared histories and futures while imagining food systems where producers and community members reclaim a central role.
